{number: 129}
{title: This Is My Father’s World}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] This is my Father's [Bb7] world,
And [Eb] to my listening [Bb7] ears
All [Eb] nature [Ab] sings, and [Eb] round me [Cm] rings
The [Fm] music [Bb7] of the [Eb] spheres.
This is my Father's [Bb7] world:
I [Eb] rest me in the [Bb7] thought
Of [Eb] rocks and [Ab] trees, of [Eb] skies and [Cm] seas;
His [Fm] hand the [Bb7] wonders [Eb] wrought.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Eb] This is my Father's [Bb7] world:
The [Eb] birds their carols [Bb7] raise,
The [Eb] morning [Ab] light, the [Eb] lily [Cm] white,
De-[Fm] clare their [Bb7] Maker's [Eb] praise.
This is my Father's [Bb7] world:
He [Eb] shines in all that's [Bb7] fair;
In the [Eb] rustling [Ab] grass I [Eb] hear Him [Cm] pass,
He [Fm] speaks to [Bb7] me every-[Eb] where.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Eb] This is my Father's [Bb7] world:
O [Eb] let me ne'er for-[Bb7] get
That [Eb] though the [Ab] wrong seems [Eb] oft so [Cm] strong,
God [Fm] is the [Bb7] Ruler [Eb] yet.
This is my Father's [Bb7] world:
Why [Eb] should my heart be [Bb7] sad?
The [Eb] Lord is [Ab] King: let the [Eb] heavens [Cm] ring!
God [Fm] reigns; let [Bb7] earth be [Eb] glad!
{end_of_verse}
